diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 634ec1f..e45a0bb 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -20,4 +20,16 @@
     Example: mini-asm -t arm -l
   
+  ### Command line (elf target)
+
+    When an assembled program starts, it receives its command line in the
+    registers, counting the command itself:
+
+      D0   number of arguments (argc)
+      A0   pointer to the argument array: 32-bit pointers to NUL-terminated
+           strings, [A0] = the command, [A0+4] = first argument, ...,
+           ending with a 0 pointer
+
+    The x86 PE and ARM targets don't pass the command line yet.
+
   ### Feedback
 
